  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "James F. “Cy” Devenny was a Seattle maritime operator who controlled Puget Sound Excursion Company and ran a fleet of passenger vessels. He operated Virginia V and Virginia VI on sightseeing routes and acquired El Primero and Aquilo. His investment in conversions and maintenance helped several ageing steam-era ships survive beyond their expected commercial lives.",
    "html": "<p>James F. “Cy” Devenny was a Seattle maritime operator who controlled Puget Sound Excursion Company and ran a fleet of passenger vessels. He operated Virginia V and Virginia VI on sightseeing routes and acquired El Primero and Aquilo. His investment in conversions and maintenance helped several ageing steam-era ships survive beyond their expected commercial lives.</p>\r\n",
